# Never let a statement anywhere near this repository.
# These patterns are deliberately broad: the cost of ignoring a file you wanted
# is one line in `git add -f`, and the cost of committing one you did not is
# permanent, because git keeps history forever.
*.csv
*.xls
*.xlsx
*.xlsm
*.pdf
*.ofx
*.qif
Statement*
statement*
*_Statement_*
*Locked*
*locked*

# Build archives and local scratch
*.zip
*.bak
*.orig
*.log
node_modules/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Working documents and notes. These quote real figures from real statements
# while they are being written, so they are excluded by type rather than by
# remembering to check each one. Word's lock files (~$...) go too.
*.docx
*.doc
*.pptx
*.rtf
~$*

# A repository GitHub Desktop once created by mistake inside this folder,
# because its dialog appends the repository name to the path you give it.
my-spending-pattern/

# Personal convenience files, not part of the project.
# The launcher is a Windows shortcut for opening the app from disk; the root
# .htaccess belongs to the dsandai.com domain rather than to this app.
Open My Spending Pattern.bat
root-htaccess-for-dsandai.txt

# Notes to myself rather than documentation of the project: launch costs and
# app-store pricing, my own cPanel runbook, and where my branding lives. None
# of it helps someone reading or running the code, so it stays local.
PUBLISHING.md
DEPLOY-cPanel.md
EDITING.md
